## Browser automation = `una` CLI

Use the `una` CLI (CDP-based, no Playwright/Puppeteer) for any browser task:
opening pages, snapping refs, clicking, checking state, screenshots.

First: `export PATH="$HOME/Library/Application Support/reflex/bun/bin:$PATH"` so
`una` resolves. Start the daemon once per session, then call verbs:

```
una serve &
una open <url>          # navigate
una snap                # snapshot → @refs (@e3 button "Increment")
una click <ref>         # click @e3
una type <ref> <text>
una check 'text="Clicks: 1"'    # assert → {verdict, rule, actual}
una batch '["open ...","snap -c","check ..."]'   # multi-step one process
```

- Start the daemon first; without it each call spawns a fresh Chrome and no
  state persists between calls.
- Always re-`snap` after a state-changing action — refs go stale.
- `snap -c` = clickable filter, `snap -l` = links/subtrees, `--json` = parseable.